{
  "dom_id": "question-213493",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Consider a relation $R$ that is defined on the set $A={2,4,6}.$ Given that $R$ is symmetric, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix. \n\n**Note**: If there is not enough information to determine a particular cell's value, then select the question mark $(\\text{?}).$\n\n|  | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| $6$ | {{field-4}} | $1$ | $0$ |",
  "worked_solution": "",
